    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "import math\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler, OneHotEncoder, OrdinalEncoder\n",
    "from sklearn.compose import ColumnTransformer\n",
    "from sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\n",
    "from sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer\n",
    "\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv(\"data_clean/nyc_taxi_combined_2025_cleaned.csv")\n",
    "print(df.head())\n",
    "print(df.shape)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3d916143",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Part 1: Datetime Parsing and Temporal Feature Extraction\n",
    "\n",
    "The columns `pickup_datetime` and `dropoff_datetime` were converted from string format into pandas datetime objects using `pd.to_datetime()`.  \n",
    "This conversion enables time-based calculations and structured temporal feature extraction.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 1.1 Trip Duration\n",
    "\n",
    "Trip duration (in minutes) was computed as:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\text{trip\\_duration\\_min}\n",
    "=\n",
    "\\frac{\\text{dropoff\\_datetime} - \\text{pickup\\_datetime}}{60}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "**Purpose**\n",
    "\n",
    "- Measures actual ride time  \n",
    "- Helps analyze congestion patterns  \n",
    "- Reflects trip efficiency  \n",
    "- Influences fare structure  \n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 1.2 Pickup Hour\n",
    "\n",
    "The hour of the day was extracted from the pickup timestamp:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\text{pickup\\_hour}\n",
    "=\n",
    "\\text{hour}(\\text{pickup\\_datetime})\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "**Purpose**\n",
    "\n",
    "- Captures diurnal travel patterns  \n",
    "- Identifies rush hours  \n",
    "- Detects nighttime traffic behavior  \n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 1.3 Pickup Weekday and Weekend Indicator\n",
    "\n",
    "The weekday index (0–6) was extracted, and a binary indicator variable `is_weekend` was created:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\text{is\\_weekend}\n",
    "=\n",
    "\\begin{cases}\n",
    "1 & \\text{if Saturday or Sunday} \\\\\n",
    "0 & \\text{otherwise}\n",
    "\\end{cases}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "**Purpose**\n",
    "\n",
    "- Distinguishes weekday commuting from weekend travel  \n",
    "- Accounts for structural differences in demand  \n",
    "- Captures variation in fare and volume patterns  \n",
    "\n",
    "---"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "ad840afe",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Parsing datetime columns\n",
    "df['pickup_datetime'] = pd.to_datetime(df['pickup_datetime'])\n",
    "df['dropoff_datetime'] = pd.to_datetime(df['dropoff_datetime'])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Trip Duration\n",
    "df['trip_duration_min'] = (\n",
    "    (df['dropoff_datetime'] - df['pickup_datetime'])\n",
    "    .dt.total_seconds() / 60\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Pickup Hour\n",
    "df['pickup_hour'] = df['pickup_datetime'].dt.hour\n",
    "\n",
    "# Pickup Day\n",
    "df['pickup_weekday'] = df['pickup_datetime'].dt.weekday\n",
    "\n",
    "df['is_weekend'] = df['pickup_weekday'].isin([5,6]).astype(int)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8f1cce41",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 2. Derived Economic Efficiency Features\n",
    "\n",
    "Several ratio-based features were engineered to improve interpretability and capture economic efficiency.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 2.1 Fare per Mile\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\text{fare\\_per\\_mile}\n",
    "=\n",
    "\\frac{\\text{fare\\_amount}}{\\text{trip\\_distance}}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "This feature measures pricing efficiency per unit distance and helps identify variations in fare structures.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 2.2 Fare per Minute\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\text{fare\\_per\\_min}\n",
    "=\n",
    "\\frac{\\text{fare\\_amount}}{\\text{trip\\_duration\\_min}}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "This variable captures pricing relative to time spent in transit and reflects congestion-related pricing dynamics.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 2.3 Tip Ratio\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\text{tip\\_ratio}\n",
    "=\n",
    "\\frac{\\text{tip\\_amount}}{\\text{total\\_amount}}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "This feature standardizes tipping behavior relative to total payment, allowing behavioral analysis independent of trip size.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Numerical Stability Adjustment\n",
    "\n",
    "To prevent division-by-zero errors and ensure numerical stability, a small constant $10^{-6}$ was added to denominators when constructing ratio-based features."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "d00039d4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Fare per Mile\n",
    "df['fare_per_mile'] = df['fare_amount'] / (df['trip_distance'] + 1e-6)\n",
    "\n",
    "#  Fare per Minute\n",
    "df['fare_per_min'] = df['fare_amount'] / (df['trip_duration_min'] + 1e-6)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Tip Ratio\n",
    "df['tip_ratio'] = df['tip_amount'] / (df['total_amount'] + 1e-6)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ffb3a8e9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 3. Feature Grouping by Data Type\n",
    "\n",
    "To facilitate preprocessing and modeling, features were grouped according to their data types.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 3.1 Numerical Features\n",
    "\n",
    "These include continuous or count-based variables such as:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Trip distance  \n",
    "- Trip duration  \n",
    "- Fare amount and total amount  \n",
    "- Tip amount and toll amount  \n",
    "- Surcharges and taxes  \n",
    "- Passenger count  \n",
    "- Pickup hour  \n",
    "\n",
    "These variables contain quantitative information and are suitable for scaling and normalization.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 3.2 Categorical Features\n",
    "\n",
    "- `payment_type`  \n",
    "- `taxi_type`  \n",
    "\n",
    "These represent nominal categories without inherent ordering and therefore require encoding before modeling.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 3.3 Binary Feature\n",
    "\n",
    "- `is_weekend`  \n",
    "\n",
    "This variable is already numeric (0 or 1) and does not require further transformation.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "id": "9a71f390",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Group Different Feature Types\n",
    "numerical_features = [\n",
    "    'trip_distance',\n",
    "    'trip_duration_min',\n",
    "    'fare_amount',\n",
    "    'total_amount',\n",
    "    'tip_amount',\n",
    "    'tolls_amount',\n",
    "    'fare_per_mile',\n",
    "    'fare_per_min',\n",
    "    'tip_ratio',\n",
    "    'passenger_count',\n",
    "    'pickup_hour',\n",
    "    'cbd_congestion_fee',\n",
    "    'congestion_surcharge',\n",
    "    'extra',\n",
    "    'improvement_surcharge',\n",
    "    'mta_tax'\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "categorical_features = [\n",
    "    'payment_type',\n",
    "    'taxi_type'\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "binary_features = [\n",
    "    'is_weekend'\n",
    "]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2d7e8b94",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 4. Missing Value Imputation\n",
    "\n",
    "Missing values were handled using **scikit-learn’s `SimpleImputer`**.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 4.1 Numerical Variables\n",
    "\n",
    "For numerical features, the **median** was used for imputation.\n",
    "\n",
    "The median is robust to:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Outliers  \n",
    "- Skewed distributions  \n",
    "- Heavy-tailed data  \n",
    "\n",
    "These characteristics are common in taxi fare and trip duration data.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 4.2 Categorical Variables\n",
    "\n",
    "For categorical features, the **most frequent category (mode)** was used.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Rationale\n",
    "\n",
    "This preprocessing step ensures that no missing values propagate into subsequent modeling stages, maintaining numerical stability and preventing training errors.\n",
    "\n",
    "# 5. Feature Scaling (Standardization)\n",
    "\n",
    "All numerical variables were standardized using **StandardScaler**, which transforms each feature as:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "z = \\frac{x - \\mu}{\\sigma}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "where:\n",
    "\n",
    "- $\\mu$ is the mean  \n",
    "- $\\sigma$ is the standard deviation  \n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Justification\n",
    "\n",
    "- Variables such as trip distance and total amount operate on very different scales.  \n",
    "- Standardization prevents large-magnitude variables from dominating model behavior.  \n",
    "- It improves numerical stability and convergence in many machine learning algorithms.  \n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# 6. Categorical Encoding (Ordinal Encoding)\n",
    "\n",
    "Categorical variables were encoded using **OrdinalEncoder**.\n",
    "\n",
    "Each category is mapped to an integer value:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\text{Category}_i \\rightarrow k\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "where $k \\in \\{0, 1, 2, \\dots\\}$ represents the encoded integer label.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Rationale\n",
    "\n",
    "- Converts categorical variables into numerical form required by most machine learning algorithms.  \n",
    "- Preserves distinct category identities.  \n",
    "- Computationally efficient compared to one-hot encoding when cardinality is low.  \n",
    "\n",
    "---"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "7fc5d02f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Standardize Numerical Features and One-Hot Encode Categorical Features\n",
    "numeric_transformer = Pipeline(steps=[\n",
    "    ('imputer', SimpleImputer(strategy='median')),\n",
    "    ('scaler', StandardScaler())\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "categorical_transformer = Pipeline(steps=[\n",
    "    ('imputer', SimpleImputer(strategy='most_frequent')),\n",
    "    ('ordinal', OrdinalEncoder())\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "preprocessor = ColumnTransformer(\n",
    "    transformers=[\n",
    "        ('num', numeric_transformer, numerical_features),\n",
    "        ('cat', categorical_transformer, categorical_features)\n",
    "    ]\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2395ca12",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 7. ColumnTransformer Pipeline Design\n",
    "\n",
    "The preprocessing steps were organized using a **ColumnTransformer** within a scikit-learn **Pipeline** framework.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Design Structure\n",
    "\n",
    "This design:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Separates numerical and categorical transformations  \n",
    "- Applies scaling only to numerical features  \n",
    "- Applies encoding only to categorical features  \n",
    "- Ensures consistent transformation across the entire dataset  \n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Advantages\n",
    "\n",
    "- Improves modularity and clarity  \n",
    "- Enhances reproducibility  \n",
    "- Reduces risk of data leakage  \n",
    "- Maintains a clean, structured preprocessing workflow  \n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# 8. Reconstruction of the Processed Dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "After applying the preprocessing pipeline:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Feature names were retrieved  \n",
    "- The transformed NumPy array was converted back into a pandas DataFrame  \n",
    "- The binary feature `is_weekend` was appended manually  \n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Final Output\n",
    "\n",
    "The final processed dataset contains:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Standardized numerical features  \n",
    "- Encoded categorical features  \n",
    "- Binary indicator variables  \n",
    "\n",
    "This structured dataset is fully prepared for subsequent modeling and analysis stages."
   ]
  },
